## Check CI status (without `gh` CLI auth)

`gh` is NOT authenticated on this Windows host. Repo is public — use the
GitHub REST API directly:

```powershell
# List recent runs
curl.exe -sS "https://api.github.com/repos/Sonlak/netconsole/actions/runs?per_page=10" ^
  | python "D:/NetConsole/.tmp-cfg/gh-runs.py"

# Get jobs/steps for one run
curl.exe -sS "https://api.github.com/repos/Sonlak/netconsole/actions/runs/<RUN_ID>/jobs" ^
  | python "D:/NetConsole/.tmp-cfg/gh-jobs.py"
```

**PowerShell gotchas:** `curl` is aliased to `Invoke-WebRequest` (no `-sS`) — use `curl.exe` explicitly. No `head` — use `python -c` or `Select-Object -First N`.

Helper scripts live in `.tmp-cfg/` (untracked, excluded from VPS rsync).

